Flashnack is a web port of LoFi Logic (flashback-raw-editor),
https://github.com/lofilogic/flashback-raw-editor, made by LoFi Logic and
licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3. Flashnack is
licensed under the same licence; see LICENSE.

Ported from LoFi Logic (GPL-3.0), each file says what it came from and what
changed:
  - the colour pipeline: ForwardMatrix, highlight recovery, white balance and
    tint, ACEScct, tone curves, V1 negative develop (core/processor.py,
    core/v1_negative.py, core/config.py)
  - every render stage and its order (core/processor.py, core/effects.py,
    core/kernels.py, core/gpu.py)
  - the WGSL compute shaders in src/gpu/shaders, copied unchanged apart from a
    header (core/shaders)
  - the five looks and their settings (core/config.py VIBE_PRESETS)
  - the 3D LUTs in public/luts, converted from assets/luts/*.cube to binary
  - the film grain tiles in public/grain (assets/grain)
  - export file names (core/export_naming.py)

Film looks added in Flashnack 0.2.0 (public/luts/look, details in
public/luts/LICENSES/README.md):
  - fb-*.png: the six looks of the Flashback camera app (Gold, Classic, Dispo,
    Beta, Cine, Retro Haze). They are Flashback's own work, copied unchanged,
    and are not covered by Flashnack's GPL licence.
  - t3-*.png: t3mujinpack by João Almeida, MIT licence
    (https://github.com/t3mujin/t3mujinpack), resampled to 64³.
  - rt-*.png: RawTherapee film simulation HaldCLUTs by Pat David, Pavlov
    Dmitry and Michael Ezra, via https://github.com/NatronGitHub/clut,
    CC BY-SA 4.0; the converted files are shared under the same licence.
  - ig-*.png: rendered from CSSgram by Una Kravets, MIT licence
    (https://github.com/una/CSSgram).
  - own-*.png: Flashnack's own, GPL-3.0.
Film, filter and brand names in the look names only say what a look aims to
resemble; no affiliation with the trademark owners is implied.

The 3D camera is Flashnack's own model, built in code from published sizes and
photos of the ONE35 V2; it leaves off Flashback's logo. The camera mode's body
is Flashnack's own art; its layout idea comes from (Not Boring) Camera.

Flashnack is not affiliated with LoFi Logic or with Flashback (joinflashback.co).
"Flashback" and "ONE35" are names of Flashback's camera products, used here only
to say which files Flashnack opens.

